1
00:00:08,832 --> 00:00:13,670
The columns on this board are not a
fact about work. They are a choice this

2
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:14,637
workspace made.

3
00:00:15,090 --> 00:00:22,620
Behind them is a task type: the steps a
job takes here, and the order it takes them

4
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:22,892
in.

5
00:00:23,344 --> 00:00:28,539
You can read the whole thing in a line,
which is the point: nobody should have to

6
00:00:28,539 --> 00:00:30,078
guess what happens next.

7
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:35,543
If your trade is a common one, somebody
has already drawn it. Pick it from the

8
00:00:35,543 --> 00:00:36,057
library.

9
00:00:36,509 --> 00:00:42,553
What you get is your own copy. Change it
however you like — no other workspace is

10
00:00:42,553 --> 00:00:43,150
touched.

11
00:00:43,603 --> 00:00:48,061
Or build one from nothing, if
the way you work is your own.

12
00:00:48,515 --> 00:00:53,788
And the jobs already on the board can be
moved onto the new steps, rather than left

13
00:00:53,788 --> 00:00:55,249
behind on the old ones.

14
00:00:55,701 --> 00:00:59,927
Next: the work that
comes round again by itself.

